<en-export export-date="20261005T031500Z" application="Evernote" version="10.105.4">
  <note>
    <title>Overnight chia pudding</title>
    <created>20260824T044000Z</created>
    <updated>20261005T031500Z</updated>
    <tag>breakfast</tag>
    <tag>meal-prep</tag>
    <tag>high-protein</tag>
    <note-attributes>
      <author>David Barron</author>
    </note-attributes>
    <content>
      <![CDATA[<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no"?>
<!DOCTYPE en-note SYSTEM "http://xml.evernote.com/pub/enml2.dtd">
<en-note><div>For the SF fridge (shared kitchen, label the jar!). 4 servings.</div><div><br/></div><ul><li>1/2 cup chia seeds</li><li>2 cups unsweetened soy milk</li><li>1 cup nonfat greek yogurt</li><li>2 scoops vanilla protein</li><li>2 tbsp maple</li><li>vanilla, pinch salt</li></ul><div><br/></div><div>Whisk, rest 10 min, whisk again (prevents clumps), fridge overnight. Top with berries.</div><div><br/></div><div>Per serving: 330 kcal, 27 g protein, 26 g carbs, 13 g fat.</div><div><br/></div><div>10/4: dropped the maple to 1 tbsp and added 1/2 cup canned pumpkin + pumpkin spice for the fall version. per serving now ~315 kcal. taper week = less sugar anyway.</div></en-note>]]>
    </content>
  </note>
</en-export>
